From: allolive <160342668+allolive@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 20:30:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] Blu-ray 3D: put the second view on title time, as the base
 view

The demuxer puts a Blu-ray's packets on title time from the clip they
were read in, so a seamless join does not step the timestamps back.
Playlists with a 3D second view were left out, as the second view's
demuxer converted its timestamps on its own. Their joins still stepped
back and were corrected in the player by dts. A clip whose first
picture carries no DTS of its own has its dts a frame late, so the next
clip landed a frame early, its first picture on the last one's pts: a
picture dropped at each join, and at some the decoder's output held.

The second view's demuxer now converts its timestamps as the base
view's are, from its play item's in time and start in the title, so the
two views stay paired and the joins of a 3D playlist go on as a 2D
one's. Both views take the conversion from one function, so they cannot
drift apart. In navigation mode, where the base view is not on title time,
the second view is not either.

Signed-off-by: allolive <160342668+allolive@users.noreply.github.com>
